WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.030
A ball rolls down a ramp,
picking up speed as it goes.

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.650
To measure speed, you need two moments:
how far it travels between them,

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.580
and how long that takes.

4
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:14.500
But at exactly three seconds,
the ball is at one point,

5
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:15.960
at one moment.

6
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:19.280
So what could its speed at
that single instant mean?

7
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.220
Is there even such a thing?

8
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.700
In this mission, you'll draw chords and
tangents on a distance against time graph,

9
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.590
and work out their gradients.

10
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.630
And you'll meet a new piece
of notation, d y by d x,

11
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.050
also written f dash of x.

12
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.350
Your mission: decide what your
speed at one instant really is.
